reviews.strengths:
The fix is in the right place. The AI's guess at 'can this unit still charge after it Advances' was a text match. It is replaced with EffectPrimitivesData.has_effect_advance_and_charge, the check ChargePhase and ChargeMove11e actually use at 11e (their adrenaline term returns false at 11e). It covers all three places where the text match was used (the chase gate, _should_unit_advance and _should_unit_advance_long_trip), and grep finds no other copy.

Param 0 restores the base exactly. The off branch returns flag or text, as before. The new log lines can only print when the new answer differs from the old one, so they stay silent at 0. No debug log was removed.

Real grants are kept:
- the War Cry flag;
- Kult of Speed SPEED FREEKS;
- the SW 11e Assault doctrine (s7442 checked: sw11e_doctrine 'assault', so it stays unchanged);
- Custodes stratagems and enhancements;
- Turbo Engine.

The patch is small and does not depend on the keeper release. It applies cleanly to V9 and to V9R (5f3485a), with offsets only. The cost is negligible: the predicate runs once per unit per plan for the long trip, once per assignment for the chase gate, and per candidate only inside the 2" window. The engine hooks have no logging side effects.

The decision checks match the code for s7468 (a genuine lost charge: Waaagh! already used, no source to rile the unit up), s7472, s7473, s7442 and the round-1 Lootas guardrails. By code reading, s7470 is untouched. The fix also corrects real bench errors: bench Stormboyz carry Full Throttle text the engine never grants, and bench Blade Champions carry Martial Inspiration text, so the base AI Advances both into lost charges all game. The test pins and erases the override and fails on base for the right reason.
